(7363316, 1152181, 8759, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mariuca:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by markwiley:</b></div><hr/><i> Fantastic shot. Only distraction -- haloing around the bodies. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I concur - no need to sharpen again after saving for the web. Or use selective sharpening </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>The haloing around the bodies is in the original unedited version as well. The BW just emphasises it. It''s just a point an shot camera...<br/>I struggled to get rid of it and there is no extra sharpen applied.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2015-06-15 11:28:44.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by mariuca: Originally posted by markwiley: Fantastic shot. Only distraction -- haloing around the bodies.   I concur - no need to sharpen again after saving for the web. Or use selective sharpening   The haloing around the bodies is in the original unedited version as well. The BW just emphasises it. It''s just a point an shot camera...I struggled to get rid of it and there is no extra sharpen applied.', '2015-06-15 12:27:26.000000', '2015-06-15 12:28:44.000000', 0),
