(7368345, 1152110, 113016, '<td valign="top">this is wonderful.</td>', 'this is wonderful.', '2015-06-21 14:53:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(7370537, 1152178, 46918, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club...<br/> <br/>To tell you the truth I had to look up who Mary Ellen Mark was before I critiqued this pic. I think you matched her style nicely. I agree with your comment about the pic being skewed. That to me is a bit distracting but it didn''t seem to hurt your score. I really like the man looking directly at the camera. I think that adds tons of interest for me. To be quite honest I have no negatives for you. (That''s a good thing I hope) Congrats on the ribbon. In my opinion well deserved. Happy shooting</td>', 'Hello from the critique club... To tell you the truth I had to look up who Mary Ellen Mark was before I critiqued this pic. I think you matched her style nicely. I agree with your comment about the pic being skewed. That to me is a bit distracting but it didn''t seem to hurt your score. I really like the man looking directly at the camera. I think that adds tons of interest for me. To be quite honest I have no negatives for you. (That''s a good thing I hope) Congrats on the ribbon. In my opinion well deserved. Happy shooting', '2015-06-23 15:10:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(7370553, 1152214, 46918, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club...<br/> <br/>In your comments you say that you had some shots with fewer people, personally in this case I like the more children. Each of the children''s faces tells a different story. I can only imagine what the girl on the right is thinking. I think this is a nicely done black &amp; white. You were able to bring out the textures in the stone / concrete on the right. I think you scored about right 6.2 is not a bad score at all.... Happy shooting</td>', 'Hello from the critique club... In your comments you say that you had some shots with fewer people, personally in this case I like the more children. Each of the children''s faces tells a different story. I can only imagine what the girl on the right is thinking. I think this is a nicely done black & white. You were able to bring out the textures in the stone / concrete on the right. I think you scored about right 6.2 is not a bad score at all.... Happy shooting', '2015-06-23 15:35:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(7370559, 1152217, 46918, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club...<br/> <br/>I think you did an ok job matching Mark''s style. These challenges are always hard to match the styles. There is a well defined subject....good DOF...Nice lighting. This ends up making a nice black &amp; white. Good job</td>', 'Hello from the critique club... I think you did an ok job matching Mark''s style. These challenges are always hard to match the styles. There is a well defined subject....good DOF...Nice lighting. This ends up making a nice black & white. Good job', '2015-06-23 15:53:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(7370701, 1152268, 46918, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club...<br/> <br/>I like the amount of detail in your shot. I also think it follows the challenge very closely. It''s nice but I think it scored about right. It is definitely a very caring / loving image. Good job</td>', 'Hello from the critique club... I like the amount of detail in your shot. I also think it follows the challenge very closely. It''s nice but I think it scored about right. It is definitely a very caring / loving image. Good job', '2015-06-23 18:07:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(7371794, 1151577, 46918, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club...<br/> <br/>As far as the quality of the b&amp;w it''s a nice shot. Your dof is good. Your subject is well defined. Unlike your other comment I don''t have a problem with the way he is looking. Looking towards the left does not bother me at all. The problem I do notice is the bicycle. I think in the location it''s in is a bit distracting. Mainly the handlebars by his head. I think it would have done much better if he was in front of the bike. I still think the bike is necessary for your shot....I just would have chosen a different location. Overall nice shot though. Happy shooting...</td>', 'Hello from the critique club... As far as the quality of the b&w it''s a nice shot. Your dof is good. Your subject is well defined. Unlike your other comment I don''t have a problem with the way he is looking. Looking towards the left does not bother me at all. The problem I do notice is the bicycle. I think in the location it''s in is a bit distracting. Mainly the handlebars by his head. I think it would have done much better if he was in front of the bike. I still think the bike is necessary for your shot....I just would have chosen a different location. Overall nice shot though. Happy shooting...', '2015-06-24 13:01:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(7400941, 1152101, 98339, '<td valign="top">I can''t tell you how many times I would go swimming on our horse farm in the watering tanks.  Mind you we had a swimming pool but that didn''t distract from the lovely green glowing slime in the tanks...nope not one bit...lol  Great picture...soooo well done!!!</td>', 'I can''t tell you how many times I would go swimming on our horse farm in the watering tanks.  Mind you we had a swimming pool but that didn''t distract from the lovely green glowing slime in the tanks...nope not one bit...lol  Great picture...soooo well done!!!', '2015-08-30 12:28:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(7408522, 1152181, 8759, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tnun:</b></div><hr/><i> astonishing. it is a cross between soviet realism and a David Hockney painting, with tons of hybrid vigour. worth at least 12. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks! <br/> <br/>Can we name it Romanian realism ;)</td>', 'Originally posted by tnun: astonishing. it is a cross between soviet realism and a David Hockney painting, with tons of hybrid vigour. worth at least 12.   Thanks!  Can we name it Romanian realism ;)', '2015-10-07 02:49:27.000000', NULL, 0);
